A||||17||RossT||whats it worth (88gt t-top)||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||04-27-2000||12:26 AM||||I have found another fiero that I am interested in, and would like your opinions on what it is worth.<P>88gt<BR>t-tops<BR>white<BR>5-speed<BR>gold wheel package<BR>tan cloth interior<BR>lumbar<BR>eq radio with subwoofer<BR>rear wing<BR>(no rear defog)<P>the car has 18,040 miles on, stored in the winter.  The car needs nothing (yet) and is in excellent shape.  The rpo codes all match except it does not have the "CJB" code for the t-top.  After a little research I found that the dealership took the car off their lot and sent it to C&C for t-tops instalation. Then the dealer sold it new to the current owner.  I have been told that not having the CJB code will cut its value by<BR>$2,000 to $3,000 dollars, even though it is still a C&C job.<P>For those of you that go to fiero shows and see alot of these cars, I would like your input.  Thanks.<P>Ross<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||04-27-2000||01:42 AM||||just buy it!  It has lumbar!  I think only 300 some 88's had it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||04-27-2000||02:13 AM||||Standard, if I do buy it I will be driving thru MSP on the way home. I'll swing by so we can get a pic of our gt's together....<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||04-27-2000||02:32 AM||||Really?  That's be awesome!  I'm afraid my GT will probably look pretty ratty next to that one, considering mine has nearly 130,000 more miles on it..   when do you think you'd be up here?||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||04-27-2000||03:19 AM||||Standard, I would be shooting for May 13,14.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=743228&a=5406255&p=20239745" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=743228&a=5406255&p=20239745</A> <P>But I am still trying to figure out if this is worth what the guy is asking.  I will most<BR>likely buy it anyway.  Heck only 300 lumbar made in 88!! I guy could not go wrong with that. I will let you know.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88 Database Nut||04-27-2000||08:13 AM||||Whoa there RossT, from Mark Corbin's spotter guide there are 861 GTs in '88 with lumbar.  I agree it's rare, but it's not 300. The number of gold wheels optioned cars is not known, but it's a pretty small number, probably on the same order as the Lumbar.  Combining these with the ttops makes it a rare beast, not withstanding them being "aftermarket" ttops.  Having said all that, have you checked out ALL the online sites for 88s?  Autotrader.com has 144 as of today, Classifieds2000.com has a bunch, cars.com, autoweb.com, usedcars.com, yahoo.com all have cars galore.  I don't know what he is asking, but I don't think the TTops not being factory devalues it by that much.  If it was a near zero mile car that you were going to keep that way, and it was going to be put up for sale as a low mileage collectible to an audience of collectors, then it might matter, but for general sales it isn't that big a deal, maybe $500 if not less.  I mean, when you sell it, would you want to knock $2500 off because of that?  8)  <BR>After saying all that, it looks Beautiful!  If it makes you happy and you can afford it, then it's worth every penny.  I hope you get it and enjoy the hell out of it.<BR>Good Luck, Happy TTOPing!  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||04-27-2000||09:48 AM||||Thanks database, standard and I were kind of joking around with the 300 fiqure.  The 800 plus sounds about right. If you had to guess a price range for such a car, what would it be? I will send you the vin for your database.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Database Nut||04-27-2000||10:37 AM||||No prob T, hope I didn't step on your toes, just trying to give you some numbers.<BR>Price, hard to say.  From Autotrader.com, here's some examples of TTops.<BR>GT 9k miles, $15500<BR>GT 25k        11800<BR>?  80k        11000  has turbo<BR>GT 45k         8950<BR>FO 48k         5250<BR>FO 113k        2100   on yahoo auction.<P>Check out Cooter's thread about the 88GT TTOP<BR>for sale in his area for $1900.  Prob has some issues and won't be low miles (maybe, maybe not), but there are DEALs out there.  Occaisionally there are low mile cars sold by non-enthusiasts for 5-6000 bucks.  I would suggest that you set an amount you want to spend and then either try to talk the guy down to your number's neighborhood or keep looking until you find the car you want.  There is no doubt in my mind that a little while after you buy this one, you'll see a better deal.  But, sometimes you do what you gotta do right?  and so what if you didn't get the lowest price, if it makes you happy.<BR>Best of Luck, thanks for the VIN help! 4 to go and we'll hit 4% of the 26402 out there.  I hope to get A Bunch at the swap meet this weekend.||||reg||1
